# The root CAs the board trusts for its server, hymnboard.sonrise.io.
#
# The board checks the server's certificate chain and name against these, and
# nothing else (see src/tls.cpp). They cover every CA Cloudflare issues edge
# certificates from (Google Trust Services, Let's Encrypt and SSL.com, plus
# Sectigo for backup certificates; see Cloudflare's cfssl_trust bundle). Let's
# Encrypt is also here so the server could move off Cloudflare to its own
# Let's Encrypt certificate without an OTA update first. Each is the copy in
# Mozilla's root store. Missing the root of a certificate the
# server switches to would cut the boards off until a USB visit, so
# .github/workflows/check-tls-roots.yml checks the live certificate chains
# against this file every day.
#
# Each certificate needs a "# Name:" line above it: the firmware logs which
# root a handshake used. cmake/embed_roots.py turns this file into DER for
# the firmware.

# Name: GTS Root R4
